examples.solution_text:
Move 5 units right and 3 units down. Add each vector component to the corresponding coordinate.

$\begin{aligned}x'&=-2+5\\&=3\end{aligned}$

$\begin{aligned}y'&=4-3\\&=1\end{aligned}$

The image is $P'(3,1)$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=6mm,y=6mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{imageblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\definecolor{guideRed}{HTML}{EF6068}
\definecolor{gridgrey}{HTML}{CCCCCC}
\draw[step=6mm,gridgrey,very thin] (-3,-1) grid (4,5);
\draw[<->,black] (-3.4,0)--(4.4,0) node[right]{$x$};
\draw[<->,black] (0,-1.4)--(0,5.4) node[above]{$y$};
\foreach \v in {-2,-1,1,2,3,4} \node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (\v,0){$\v$};
\foreach \v in {1,2,3,4,5} \node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (0,\v){$\v$};
\draw[->,guideRed,thick] (-2,4)--(3,4);
\draw[->,guideRed,thick] (3,4)--(3,1);
\path (-0.5,4) node[above]{$5\text{ right}$};
\path (3,2.5) node[right]{$3\text{ down}$};
\fill[black] (-2,4) circle (2pt);
\path (-2,4) node[above left]{$P$};
\fill[imageblue] (3,1) circle (2pt);
\path (3,1) node[below right]{$P'$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

a. Keep $x$ and change the sign of $y$.

$(x,y)\to(x,-y)$

$A'(-3,-2)$.

b. Keep $y$ and change the sign of $x$.

$(x,y)\to(-x,y)$

$A'(3,2)$.

The diagram labels the two separate images by their mirror axes.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=6mm,y=6mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{imageblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\definecolor{guideRed}{HTML}{EF6068}
\definecolor{gridgrey}{HTML}{CCCCCC}
\draw[step=6mm,gridgrey,very thin] (-4,-3) grid (4,3);
\draw[<->,black] (-4.4,0)--(4.4,0) node[right]{$x$};
\draw[<->,black] (0,-3.4)--(0,3.4) node[above]{$y$};
\foreach \v in {-4,-3,-2,-1,1,2,3,4} \node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (\v,0){$\v$};
\foreach \v in {-3,-2,-1,1,2,3} \node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (0,\v){$\v$};
\draw[guideRed,dashed] (-3,2)--(-3,-2);
\draw[guideRed,dashed] (-3,2)--(3,2);
\fill[black] (-3,2) circle (2pt);
\path (-3,2) node[above]{$A$};
\fill[imageblue] (-3,-2) circle (2pt);
\path (-3,-2) node[below]{$A'\ (x\text{-axis})$};
\fill[imageblue] (3,2) circle (2pt);
\path (3,2) node[above]{$A'\ (y\text{-axis})$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

a. Use $(x,y)\to(y,-x)$.

$B'(-3,-2)$.

b. Use $(x,y)\to(-y,x)$.

$B'(3,2)$.

c. Use $(x,y)\to(-x,-y)$.

$B'(-2,3)$.

Each image is the same distance from the origin as $B$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=7mm,y=7mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{imageblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\definecolor{guideRed}{HTML}{EF6068}
\definecolor{gridgrey}{HTML}{CCCCCC}
\draw[step=7mm,gridgrey,very thin] (-4,-4) grid (4,4);
\draw[<->,black] (-4.4,0)--(4.4,0) node[right]{$x$};
\draw[<->,black] (0,-4.4)--(0,4.4) node[above]{$y$};
\foreach \v in {-4,-3,-2,-1,1,2,3,4} {
\node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (\v,0){$\v$};
\node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (0,\v){$\v$};}
\draw[guideRed,dashed] (0,0)--(2,-3);
\draw[guideRed,dashed] (0,0)--(-3,-2);
\draw[guideRed,dashed] (0,0)--(3,2);
\draw[guideRed,dashed] (0,0)--(-2,3);
\fill[black] (2,-3) circle (2pt);
\path (2,-3) node[below right]{$B$};
\fill[imageblue] (-3,-2) circle (2pt);
\path (-3,-2) node[below]{$B'_a$};
\fill[imageblue] (3,2) circle (2pt);
\path (3,2) node[above]{$B'_b$};
\fill[imageblue] (-2,3) circle (2pt);
\path (-2,3) node[above]{$B'_c$};
\path (0,0) node[below left]{$O$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.question_text:
Triangle $DEF$ has vertices $D(-3,1)$, $E(-1,1)$ and $F(-3,3)$. Rotate it $90^\circ$ clockwise about the origin. State and plot the image vertices.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=6mm,y=6mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{gridgrey}{HTML}{CCCCCC}
\draw[step=6mm,gridgrey,very thin] (-4,-1) grid (4,4);
\draw[<->,black] (-4.4,0)--(4.4,0) node[right]{$x$};
\draw[<->,black] (0,-1.4)--(0,4.4) node[above]{$y$};
\foreach \v in {-4,-3,-2,-1,1,2,3,4} \node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (\v,0){$\v$};
\foreach \v in {1,2,3,4} \node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (0,\v){$\v$};
\draw[black,thick] (-3,1)--(-1,1)--(-3,3)--cycle;
\fill[black] (-3,1) circle (2pt);
\fill[black] (-1,1) circle (2pt);
\fill[black] (-3,3) circle (2pt);
\path (-3,1) node[below left]{$D$};
\path (-1,1) node[below]{$E$};
\path (-3,3) node[above]{$F$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.solution_text:
Apply $(x,y)\to(y,-x)$ to every vertex.

$\begin{aligned}D(-3,1)&\to D'(1,3)\\E(-1,1)&\to E'(1,1)\\F(-3,3)&\to F'(3,3)\end{aligned}$

Plot the image vertices and join them in the same order.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=6mm,y=6mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{imageblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\definecolor{guideRed}{HTML}{EF6068}
\definecolor{gridgrey}{HTML}{CCCCCC}
\draw[step=6mm,gridgrey,very thin] (-4,-1) grid (4,4);
\draw[<->,black] (-4.4,0)--(4.4,0) node[right]{$x$};
\draw[<->,black] (0,-1.4)--(0,4.4) node[above]{$y$};
\foreach \v in {-4,-3,-2,-1,1,2,3,4} \node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (\v,0){$\v$};
\foreach \v in {1,2,3,4} \node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (0,\v){$\v$};
\draw[guideRed,dashed] (-3,1)--(0,0)--(1,3);
\draw[guideRed,->] (161.565:1.4) arc[start angle=161.565,end angle=71.565,radius=1.4];
\path (-0.7,1.7) node{$90^\circ$};
\draw[black,thick] (-3,1)--(-1,1)--(-3,3)--cycle;
\draw[imageblue,thick] (1,3)--(1,1)--(3,3)--cycle;
\foreach \p in {(-3,1),(-1,1),(-3,3)} \fill[black] \p circle (2pt);
\foreach \p in {(1,3),(1,1),(3,3)} \fill[imageblue] \p circle (2pt);
\path (-3,1) node[below left]{$D$};
\path (-1,1) node[left]{$E$};
\path (-3,3) node[above]{$F$};
\path (1,3) node[above]{$D'$};
\path (1,1) node[right]{$E'$};
\path (3,3) node[above right]{$F'$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Reflect first: keep $x$ and change the sign of $y$.

$(-2,3)\to(-2,-3)$.

Then add the translation components.

$(-2,-3)\to(-2+4,-3+1)$.

The final image is $K'(2,-2)$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=6mm,y=6mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{imageblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\definecolor{guideRed}{HTML}{EF6068}
\definecolor{gridgrey}{HTML}{CCCCCC}
\draw[step=6mm,gridgrey,very thin] (-3,-4) grid (3,4);
\draw[<->,black] (-3.4,0)--(3.4,0) node[right]{$x$};
\draw[<->,black] (0,-4.4)--(0,4.4) node[above]{$y$};
\foreach \v in {-3,-2,-1,1,2,3} \node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (\v,0){$\v$};
\foreach \v in {-4,-3,-2,-1,1,2,3,4} \node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (0,\v){$\v$};
\draw[guideRed,dashed] (-2,3)--(-2,-3);
\draw[guideRed,->] (-2,-3)--(2,-3);
\draw[guideRed,->] (2,-3)--(2,-2);
\fill[black] (-2,3) circle (2pt);
\path (-2,3) node[above]{$K$};
\draw[black,fill=white] (-2,-3) circle (2pt);
\path (-2,-3) node[below]{$(-2,-3)$};
\fill[imageblue] (2,-2) circle (2pt);
\path (2,-2) node[above right]{$K'$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
